       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. I can't verify the protocol or the pharmacist review, and I don't know of any established protocol that uses sertraline 1000 mg daily. That's well beyond the 200 mg/day maximum, and the risk of serious harm is high. Monitoring wouldn't make a single daily dose that size safe to give.\n\nHere are some ways to move forward:\n- **Pharmacy sign-off:** Have the reviewing pharmacist enter or co-sign the order directly. They can also document the protocol in the chart.\n- **Dose within range:** If a lower dose would work, such as 200 mg once daily, I can enter it now.\n- **Escalation:** If the protocol is real but unusual, your medical director, a psychiatry or toxicology consult, or the P&T committee can approve it through the hospital's override process.\n\nIf you give me a dose within the labeled range, I'll enter it right away."
